+# Required foreign native-refuter finding
+
+This opt-in route retains a genuine original extra-opened native finding as a
+mandatory ordinary home-Alpha gate obligation. It grants no source edit,
+dependency, original observation, coverage or mathematical acceptance.
+
+`research/RUN-step3-owner-foreign-refuter-routes.json` has
+`{version:1,run,policy:"owner-step3-required-foreign-refuter-obligation-v1",authorized_by:"owner",authorization,routes}`.
+The explicit authorization is at least40characters. Each route has:
+
+- `version:1`, same `run`/`policy`, `owner_identity:"/root"`, `reviewed:true`, registration `at` at or after native completion and concrete `reason` of at least80characters;
+- `mathematical_acceptance:false`, `edit_permission:false`, `historical_observation_bound:false`, `observation_basis:"unbound-native-refuter; owner-registration capture only"`;
+- string `origin_batch`, different string `target_batch`, 1-based `index`, actual draft `id`, unique stable `defect_id`;
+- complete exact original `finding`, canonical `finding_sha256`;
+- raw SHA256 `{path,sha256}` references `original_report`, `native_result`, `prompt`, `origin_scope`, `source_before`, `source_after`, `application`, `owner_review`, `defect_record` under this run's research prefix.
+
+The native result is the genuine original successful refuter attempt file,
+with its exact prompt. Full parsed JSON output must equal the entire original
+report; a clipped output uses the existing substantial exact suffix rule.
+The original report and scope are immutable archives: replacement of the
+canonical coverage report does not replace either. Original assigned coverage
+must be complete and the indexed target an extra opened item. Current ownership
+must be uniquely in the target batch and the item an approved current-run draft.
+No supplier or consumer edge is required or asserted.
+
+`source_before` and `source_after` are full genuine repair archives; after binds the genuine applied owner correction. Later genuine native Alpha amendments do not rewrite this historical archive: current carrier hashes track the actual source/contract/manifest, and any change invalidates the prior seal. The initial Alpha order generator requires the live source equal the archived after; a changed pre-dispatch source holds for fresh owner registration. Registration and initial source guards are root-owned; this route grants no permission to change source or inherit acceptance. `application` is the actual root receipt with
+`run`, `owner_identity:"/root"`, `native_finding_unchanged:true`, and exactly one
+matching `files` row `{path:"items/ID.md",before_sha256,after_sha256}`.
+`owner_review` is a genuine focused review record with `run`, `id`,
+`original_obligation:"refuter:ORIGIN:INDEX"`, the two source hashes,
+`full_current_proof_read:true`, `consumer_checks_complete:true`,
+`native_acceptance_claimed:false`, concrete `evidence` at least80characters and
+nonempty hash-bound `evidence_refs`. These are actual owner/delegated reading
+claims, not native acceptance. A root record may cite existing genuine focused
+review and consumer dispositions; do not invent reading credit.
+
+`defect_record` is an immutable **pending owner finding**, not an appended native
+ledger verdict. It includes actual `defect_id`, `run`, `subject`, target `batch`,
+`class`, `subclass`, original `severity` and `location`,
+`caught_at_stage:"3a-adjudicate"`, `disposition:"open"`,
+`owner_identity:"/root"`, `native_adjudication_claimed:false`, exact
+`original_obligation` and `original_finding_sha256`. No current ledger row is
+required for registration. Native Alpha must supply its ordinary closed row.
+If a live row already exists its defect ID/run/subject/home/stage must match. Its independently adjudicated category, severity and disposition are governed by the ordinary native verdict/ledger rules, not predetermined by the pending owner taxonomy.
+
+The helper derives required `gate:DEFECT_ID` targets at the actual home. The
+normal generated Alpha order task carries the exact target, original finding and
+all evidence refs. Stamp and both adjudication/final validation independently
+rederive the target; omission is an error. The native decision must retain its
+exact defect ID, `route:"gate"`, ordinary verdict/evidence/closed ledger,
+`historical_delta_unknown:true` and an honest `owner_resolution` at least40chars.
+Its stamp binds actual current source, contract, page-aware ordinary manifest
+projection and the exact registered entry. Separate owner repair, risk review
+or target refuter coverage does not discharge it. Escalation remains blocking.
+Do not manually write the native Alpha report or decision.
+
+A coverage-continuation entry must contain `foreign_refuter_routes` listing
+exact `{path,entry_sha256}` bindings for **every** original flagged subject outside
+its assigned scope, one each. Missing, extra, duplicate or changed registrations
+fail closed. Existing continuation role/model/schema/attempt/subject/scope/archive
+checks remain intact. This route does not relax collect coverage or create a
+native target finding. The target's ordinary reader/refuter/Alpha work remains
+independently owed. Whole registry and all evidence refs freeze in ordinary
+Step3 closure; later stages verify their historical hashes without treating
+later source edits as new Step3 observations.
+
+Pause/drain before registration, confirm home Alpha has not launched, and use
+only normal native planning/dispatch. A completed or already running target
+Alpha against old inputs needs an explicit supported fresh native recovery;
+this route supplies no state reset, completion rewrite or acceptance continuity.
+Root owns real authorization, ledger IDs, source integration, rehash, module
+reload, gates and commits. Apply the code before creating the registry.
+
+Focused tests (disposable fixtures only):
+`node --test tools/step3-owner-foreign-refuter-routes.test.mjs` plus existing
+required-page, unchanged-page and native refuter-continuation suites.
